{"assets":["/statement-assets/2132a595ab90d4e243e1fc4b785c634465b74185f6c693c39853b7022f2dbf72.png"],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"1446","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"C. Xor Tree"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"2 seconds"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For a given sequence of "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"distinct"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" non-negative integers $$$(b_1, b_2, \\dots, b_k)$$$ we determine if it is "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"good"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" in the following way:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" Consider a graph on $$$k$$$ nodes, with numbers from $$$b_1$$$ to $$$b_k$$$ written on them."}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" For every $$$i$$$ from $$$1$$$ to $$$k$$$: find such $$$j$$$ ($$$1 \\le j \\le k$$$, $$$j\\neq i$$$), for which $$$(b_i \\oplus b_j)$$$ "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"is the smallest"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" among all such $$$j$$$, where $$$\\oplus$$$ denotes the operation of bitwise XOR ("},{"attrs":{"href":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bitwise_operation#XOR"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bitwise_operation#XOR"}],"kind":"link"},{"kind":"text","text":"). Next, draw an "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"undirected"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" edge between vertices with numbers $$$b_i$$$ and $$$b_j$$$ in this graph."}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" We say that the sequence is "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"good"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" if and only if the resulting graph forms a "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"tree"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" (is connected and doesn't have any simple cycles). "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"It is possible that for some numbers $$$b_i$$$ and $$$b_j$$$, you will try to add the edge between them twice. Nevertheless, you will add this edge only once."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"You can find an example below (the picture corresponding to the first test case). "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Sequence $$$(0, 1, 5, 2, 6)$$$ "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"is not"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" good as we "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"cannot"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" reach $$$1$$$ from $$$5$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"However, sequence $$$(0, 1, 5, 2)$$$ "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"is"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" good. "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/statement-assets/2132a595ab90d4e243e1fc4b785c634465b74185f6c693c39853b7022f2dbf72.png"},"kind":"image"}],"kind":"container"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"You are given a sequence $$$(a_1, a_2, \\dots, a_n)$$$ of "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"distinct"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" non-negative integers. You would like to remove some of the elements (possibly none) to make the "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"remaining"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" sequence good. What is the minimum possible number of removals required to achieve this goal?"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"It can be shown that for any sequence, we can remove some number of elements, leaving at least $$$2$$$, so that the remaining sequence is good."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line contains a single integer $$$n$$$ ($$$2 \\le n \\le 200,000$$$) — length of the sequence."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The second line contains $$$n$$$ "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"distinct"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" non-negative integers $$$a_1, a_2, \\ldots, a_n$$$ ($$$0 \\le a_i \\le 10^9$$$) — the elements of the sequence."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"You should output exactly one integer — the minimum possible number of elements to remove in order to make the remaining sequence good."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Examples"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n5\n0 1 5 2 6\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n1\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n7\n6 9 8 7 3 5 2\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n2\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note that numbers which you remove "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"don't"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" impact the procedure of telling whether the resulting sequence is good."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"It is possible that for some numbers $$$b_i$$$ and $$$b_j$$$, you will try to add the edge between them twice. Nevertheless, you will add this edge only once."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"C","problemCode":"1446C","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/1446/problem/C"}